#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""DEVELOPMENT-ONLY entry point for a Development Claude Code session.

This is the official way to start Development Claude Code. It resolves the git
repository root from the source tree, refuses to run on a Production runtime,
refuses to start anywhere but a ``claude/*`` branch, and ``chdir``s to that root
immediately before ``exec claude`` -- so a human may call it from
``daytrade-sbi/`` (or anywhere else) and Claude still starts at the repository
root, where the Claude Sandbox can write ``.git`` and ``git add`` /
``git commit`` therefore work with the sandbox fully enabled.

    daytrade-sbi/scripts/claude-development

It is NOT ``scripts/claude-production``. That launcher is a separate, human-only
Production entry point with its own fail-closed runtime-security preflight; this
one has nothing to do with it and stops immediately if a Production runtime is
detected.

NOT A SECURITY BOUNDARY. This file lives in the repository and Development
Claude Code can edit it, exactly like ``scripts/claude-safe-push``. It disables
no sandbox, sets no ``allowUnsandboxedCommands``, relaxes no permission, changes
no Production Managed Policy, and touches no ``.git`` ownership or mode. Raw
``git push`` stays denied; ``scripts/claude-safe-push`` remains the only push
path.

The preflight core lives in ``src/claude_development_launcher.py`` so that it is
unit-testable; this file stays a thin entry point.
"""

from __future__ import annotations

import sys
from pathlib import Path

sys.path.insert(0, str(Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]))

from src.claude_development_launcher import main  # noqa: E402

if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main())
